# t169-macros.tsv COLUMNS (t169-guardsweep.sh)
# macro  ndef  nval  same  axis  minority  sites  i386-value  aarch64-value
#
#   ndef      how many of the 48 back ends define it, through their REAL tm.h
#             chain (cpp -dM over the generated tm-<base>.h), not a grep of
#             gcc/config/<be>/ -- elfos.h and friends sit ABOVE the back-end
#             directory and a directory grep misattributes them.
#   nval      distinct VALUES among the definers.
#   same      how many bases give byte-identically what i386 gives.  48-same is
#             the number of back ends served a foreign answer, because the
#             shared tm.h IS i386s chain.
#   axis      PRESENCE (some define, some do not) | VALUE (all define, values
#             differ) | CONVERTED (expands to mt_*() or targetm_cdata: the fix,
#             not the bug) | agree (48/48, one value).
#   minority  MINORITY if i386s answer is not the commonest one.
